From 1e9e930be039eec4bc014949912866fbe33ce39a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redux Kernel Research <redux@invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:32:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: opp: sun50i: allow turbo-mode and opp-suspend

The H6/H616 OPP binding lists the OPP node properties it accepts and
rejects everything else, so a board can't mark an OPP as a boost
frequency (turbo-mode) or as the frequency to use while suspending
(opp-suspend). Both are generic properties of opp-v2-base.yaml and the
cpufreq-dt driver honours them. Allow them.

An H700 handheld uses both: its fastest OPP is a boost frequency, off
by default, and its slowest OPP is used during suspend.

This patch was drafted with an AI coding assistant (Claude) and checked
with dt_binding_check and dtbs_check. It has not been tested on
hardware.
---
 .../bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml      | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
index 91f3b9251..a72d0148c 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/opp/allwinner,sun50i-h6-operating-points.yaml
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ patternProperties:
       opp-hz: true
       clock-latency-ns: true
       opp-microvolt: true
+      opp-suspend: true
+      turbo-mode: true
       opp-supported-hw:
         maxItems: 1
         description:
